    + skip the adorning rhetoric and go straight into the unadorned argument
        - the next major task for the argument:

            P: a practical principle of pure reason that arguably (as I shall argue later)
              is enforced and thereby absolute
                : ad `of pure reason` : what suffices for a law qua moral as giver of its principle,
                  as opposed to pure logic, which deals in morality and behaviour only *via* reason
                : re `of pure reason` cf. `^*\(-\) there is a principle of pure logic` :
                  the corresponding principle of pure logic to which reason conforms through its
                  stipulation of P, a contextual mapping of the principle from logic to reason
            : cf. `^*\+ argue for.+a stable ground of maintenance re practical logic$`
        1+ formulate P
            : see notepad:2026-10-7a,b
            ' will the perdurance of reason
        2+ state P’s premises
            : cf. `^*\+ state the premises`
            (-) there is a principle of pure logic on the formula:
                    | {direct toward}|target self-perdurance
                        !! actual (and sufficient) movement is proper to the logic
                            - necessarily it would, moreover, take the form
                              of (sufficient) hazard reduction
                            + map it in
                : see notepad:2026-10-6c : on the logic of perdurance/decreation
                - the enforcement proper to the logic of perdurance/decreation
                  is not proper to the formula/giving of the principle
                    ∴ the former is omitted on mapping the logic into the latter
                        : cf. notepad:2026-10-7a : noting a similar dichotomy (giving vs. enforcement
                          of principle) where the same logic is mapped into the context of law
                    ∵ were it included by adding, for example, a clause of ‘on pain of decreation’,
                      then non-conformance would explicitly be allowed, if not invited
                        / a director could, in other words, accept the ‘pain of decreation’
                          and still be conformant
        3+ infer P
            : see notepad:2026-10-7d,e
            : cf. `^*\?\+ how then formulate the principle\?`

